"Patient creatures have only a species identification code, no common name."
"Adults are spiny, urchin-like, black and gray, larger than golf balls."
"An adult guards its eggs until the river is safe, then softens to release the young and dies."
"Young are transparent jelly-butterflies with tendrils and a glowing blue heart."
"Outside an academic collection, the siblinghold's stream may hold the only ones on the Triplanets."
